<%- include('partials/head') %>
<section class="page-hero container about-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow hero-enter">THE PERSON BEHIND THE PROJECTS</p>
    <h1 class="hero-enter delay-1">Behind the code.<br> <span class="gold-text">Inside Skypixel.</span></h1>
    <p class="page-description hero-enter delay-2">A little about <%= creatorName %>, the ideas behind the tools, and the identity that connects them.</p>
</section>
<section class="container about-section" aria-labelledby="about-intro">
    <aside class="about-profile reveal" aria-label="<%= creatorName %>, creator of Skypixel Framework">
        <div class="about-profile-art"><span class="profile-orbit" aria-hidden="true"></span><%- include('partials/brand-logo', {size:160, altText:'Skypixel Framework SP emblem', eager:true}) %></div>
        <p class="eyebrow">CODE · CREATE · REFINE</p>
        <h2><%= creatorName %></h2>
        <p class="profile-role">Creator of Skypixel Framework</p>
        <div class="profile-stack" aria-label="Working with"><span>Java</span><span>C#</span><span>JavaScript</span></div>
        <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/<%= username %>" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Follow the work <%- icon('arrow') %></a>
    </aside>
    <div class="about-copy reveal">
        <p class="eyebrow">HELLO, I'M <%= creatorName.toUpperCase() %></p>
        <h2 id="about-intro">Curiosity is where<br> <span class="gold-text">it usually begins.</span></h2>
        <p>I build tools for the things I enjoy working with: Minecraft servers, Windows applications, and Discord communities. A project often starts with a small question — could this be easier to manage, clearer to understand, or more useful?</p>
        <p>That question can turn into a Java plugin, a C# desktop application, or a JavaScript bot. The technologies change with the problem. What connects the work is the process of taking an idea, making it work, and refining the details that people interact with.</p>
        <p>Skypixel Framework gives those ideas a shared home. Each repository has its own purpose and personality, while this website brings the collection together so you can understand what a project does and follow its progress.</p>
        <p class="about-closing">There is always more to learn, another detail to improve, and another idea waiting to become something useful.</p>
        <div class="about-actions"><a class="button button-gold" href="/projects">Explore what I'm building <%- icon('right') %></a><a class="text-link" href="/updates">Follow the updates <%- icon('arrow') %></a></div>
    </div>
</section>
<section class="container about-principles" aria-labelledby="principles-title">
    <div class="section-heading reveal"><div><p class="eyebrow">WHAT MATTERS TO ME</p><h2 id="principles-title">The thinking behind the work.</h2><p>Different projects. A few ideas I keep coming back to.</p></div></div>
    <div class="principle-grid">
        <article class="principle-card reveal"><span class="principle-icon"><%- icon('bolt') %></span><h3>Start with a purpose.</h3><p>A useful project solves a real problem. I like tools that make a setup easier, support a community, or give people more control over the things they use.</p></article>
        <article class="principle-card reveal"><span class="principle-icon"><%- icon('code') %></span><h3>Leave room to grow.</h3><p>Publishing a repository is one step in an ongoing process. New ideas, clearer documentation, and feedback can all shape what comes next.</p></article>
        <article class="principle-card reveal"><span class="principle-icon"><%- icon('spark') %></span><h3>Care for the details.</h3><p>How something feels matters alongside how it works. Clear controls, readable information, and a consistent identity help make a tool easier to enjoy.</p></article>
    </div>
    <div class="about-invitation reveal"><div><p class="eyebrow">THE NEXT IDEA</p><h2>Have something in mind?</h2><p>Explore the repositories, try a project, or share a suggestion through its GitHub issues.</p></div><a class="button button-outline" href="https://github.com/<%= username %>?tab=repositories" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Find a repository <%- icon('arrow') %></a></div>
</section>
<% const contributors=(snapshot.contributors||[]).filter(member=>member.login!==username); if(contributors.length){ %><section class="container contributor-section"><h2>Contributors</h2><div class="contributors"><% contributors.forEach(member=>{ %><a href="https://github.com/<%= member.login %>" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong><%= member.name %></strong><%- icon('arrow') %></a><% }); %></div></section><% } %>
<%- include('partials/footer') %>
